.TH PKGBASE 1 "2026-09-07" "emerald" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkgbase \- reduce an installation to base and selected packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkgbase
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ package ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkgbase
removes all installed packages except the base set and the packages named on the command line. Dependencies of the base set and named packages are retained. This is destructive and requires root privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -n, --dryrun
Show what would be removed without changing the system.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
pkgbase -n vim git
pkgbase -y
pkgbase vim git curl
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success or dry-run completion; non-zero on invalid input or removal failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgdel (1),
.BR emerald (1)
